---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     
This command is used to logs Docker into AWS ECR (Elastic Container Registry) so you can push or pull Docker images.
   13  aws ecr get-login-password --region eu-north-1 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 921876749799.dkr.ecr.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com
-------------
      breakdown command in 2 part
13.1 AWS CLI to generate a temporary authentication token for ECR.
       aws ecr get-login-password --region eu-north-1

Meaning
aws → AWS CLI tool
ecr → Elastic Container Registry service
get-login-password → Generate Docker login password/token
--region ap-south-1 → Use the Mumbai AWS region
----------------------

13.2 The pipe (|)

The pipe sends the output of the first command into the second command.

So:
AWS generated password
        ↓
Docker login command
---------------------------
13.3 This logs Docker into the ECR registry.

docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 921876749799.dkr.ecr.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com


Meaning
docker login → Authenticate Docker
--username AWS → ECR requires username literally as AWS
--password-stdin → Read password securely from stdin (pipe)
123456789012.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com → Your ECR registry URL
